id: pm-vcs-d9m8
title: Snapshot-bounded self-host artifact still grows with source size (~39 MiB/yr linear) and could approach the 50 MiB warning within a year
description: "With the bounded single-snapshot writer (pm-vcs-7ydb), selfhost.bundle is a function of source size only: measured snapshot growth over the same 30-day window was 4,037,205 -> 7,394,951 bytes (~0.106 MiB/day), dominated by accumulating tracker history files (three .agents/pm history JSONL files are among the ten largest tracked paths). Linear projection puts the artifact near ~46 MiB within a year, under but approaching the 50 MiB per-file warning. Options to evaluate when it matters: excluding .agents/pm runtime/history payload from the bundled source, compressing the archive, or trimming tracker history growth."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: bundle,growth,self-host
created_at: "2026-10-12T07:01:35.310Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T10:52:12.063Z"
author: pi-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:52:12.063Z",claude-orchestrator,"pm-vcs-7ydb closed via PR 102: the bundle no longer grows per regeneration, but the one-year source-growth projection (about 46 MiB) leaves little headroom under GitHub's 50 MiB warning. This item owns that remainder."
body: ""
